; What makes them half-pipes. A liner centred on the axle at y = -0.30 with
; r = 0.415 reaches down to y = -0.715, which is below the ground the car is
; parked on — a full tube would hang under the sills in plain view. Everything
; below y = -0.46 goes, which is 2 cm past the tub floor at -0.44: enough overlap
; that the liner's bottom edge is hidden behind the body rather than ending in
; mid-air just inside the arch lip.
[node name="BelowAxle" type="CSGBox3D" parent="WheelWells" unique_id=1700000019]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, -0.76, 0)
operation = 2
size = Vector3(2.4, 0.6, 4.6)
